                <pb facs="1176" n="1164" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg1164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3332/99: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-24T15:00:00-03:00">June 24, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 24—2:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>305. For the Under Secretary. Department’s 179, June 22, 2 p.m. I have been told
                    very confidentially that President Vargas in private conversation has expressed
                    concern over the recent frequent visits to Brazilian ports and especially to Rio
                    de Janeiro of United States naval vessels. However, as I assume that the
                    situation at Montevideo justifies it I will go ahead with these visits.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
